        #_R_678jplh9av5ubsqlbH1_ { display: flex; }
        iframe { max-width: 100vw; }
      }</style></div></div></div><p>We asked readers what they remembered about July 20, 2021, the day Milwaukee hoisted the trophy thanks to a Game 6 win over the <a data-ylk="" data-yga="{&quot;yHasCommerce&quot;:false}" href="/nba/teams/phoenix/" rel="">Phoenix Suns</a> in the NBA Finals. Here&#x27;s what you told us:</p><div class="slideshow hide-slideshow"><div class="slideshow-wrap related-side"><div class="left-nav"><button class="hidden md:block" title="Previous photo" tabindex="0" data-ylk="ct:slideshow;elm:arrow;itc:1;outcm:ct;sec:sshow;subsec:slideshow;slk:previous;" data-yga="{&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;slideshow&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;arrow&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;sshow&quot;,&quot;ySubModuleName&quot;:&quot;slideshow&quot;,&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;previous&quot;,&quot;yHasCommerce&quot;:false}"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" class="fill-white"><path d="M22.72.665a2.27 2.27 0 0 0-3.21 0L4.175 16 19.51 31.335c.442.443 1.023.665 1.604.665s1.162-.222 1.605-.665a2.27 2.27 0 0 0 0-3.21L10.596 16 22.72 3.876a2.27 2.27 0 0 0 0-3.21z"></path></svg></button></div><div class="slide-photos" id="_R_b8jplh9av5ubsqlb_"><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="true"><div class="snap-start snap-always" data-slide-index="0"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/40f7e12f115997cc6d20cd933bf92a3c71f4e8e48c334448b8a28971608a0f7f/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Ffbfb2b058ff6c7101db72e2246f290e1&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/40f7e12f115997cc6d20cd933bf92a3c71f4e8e48c334448b8a28971608a0f7f/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Ffbfb2b058ff6c7101db72e2246f290e1"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Five years ago, Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Milwaukee Bucks to their first NBA championship in 50 years after he scored 50 points in the clinching Game 6 over the Phoenix Suns. <br><br>It capped an incredible playoff run that also saw him return faster than anyone thought from a hyperextended left knee he suffered during the Eastern Conference finals. <br><br>He would deliver several masterpieces throughout the playoffs and iconic NBA Finals moments.<br><br>Scroll through this gallery for all of Giannis' highlights during the 2021 postseason.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark J. Rebilas, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="1"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/a825d43ae192119de89e1342535ab17acfbf756d16d7ad91fc32bf1238dfc9d9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1bb0c616dab516bfa4940781743f7ba1&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/a825d43ae192119de89e1342535ab17acfbf756d16d7ad91fc32bf1238dfc9d9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1bb0c616dab516bfa4940781743f7ba1"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton in the closing moments of Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. <br><br>The Bucks defeated the Suns, 109-103, to even the series.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="2"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/59a82a2d33c73b2db79f1a4c43232dc00553a737293a774a4b60fa7c3fdd7cc5/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1cedaa3e606aba34dc16a3d27587eec9&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/59a82a2d33c73b2db79f1a4c43232dc00553a737293a774a4b60fa7c3fdd7cc5/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1cedaa3e606aba34dc16a3d27587eec9"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second quarter against the Phoenix Suns during Game 4 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on Jul 14, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Jeff Hanisch, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="3"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/5fde4a257a5fcc8f10eb176cdd26f1cf074a7190c43291ff9776137da51de1fc/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fe12995180980770c50f5825bc6173466&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/5fde4a257a5fcc8f10eb176cdd26f1cf074a7190c43291ff9776137da51de1fc/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fe12995180980770c50f5825bc6173466"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Milwaukee Bucks defeated the Brooklyn Nets in overtime in Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Wendell Cruz, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="4"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/88037ce2f7d4322f509990d5ad1a1cbc7979f1dd35ac089aed86eea8a272fe37/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F518d4fbf4b0be52ec581180e5d0b1b56&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/88037ce2f7d4322f509990d5ad1a1cbc7979f1dd35ac089aed86eea8a272fe37/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F518d4fbf4b0be52ec581180e5d0b1b56"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) slams against Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) during Game 2 of the NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="5"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/681a3268877408ddf1f7cb316b1653ef4f6c2e169b668858e008994cc0f3c2bc/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F15d2f5fdf4225e1256b8d4d30f1b1790&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/681a3268877408ddf1f7cb316b1653ef4f6c2e169b668858e008994cc0f3c2bc/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F15d2f5fdf4225e1256b8d4d30f1b1790"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) takes a moment before their first-round playoff series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="6"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/5762d1ac2dff40aec0c51f1402e433c41e2af48f247b2365c8d28d283381f746/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F8b427304c08f0801491fbac0d2d26ce0&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/5762d1ac2dff40aec0c51f1402e433c41e2af48f247b2365c8d28d283381f746/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F8b427304c08f0801491fbac0d2d26ce0"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) looks on in the fourth quarter during Game 4 in the first round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Miami Heat at American Airlines Arena. <br><br>The Bucks beat the Heat, 120-103, to complete a series sweep.<br><br>Antetokounmpo posted a triple double in the clinching game, with 20 points, 12 rebounds and 15 assists.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Sam Navarro, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="7"><div class