%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F5af88c6f21dd6a3933edb393f619e2f3"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) attempts a shot as Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) defends in the first quarter during Game 5 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena on July 17, 2021.<br><br>Antetokounmpo had a team-high 32 points in the Bucks' 123-119 victory. The win put the Bucks ahead in the series, 3-2.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark J. Rebilas, Mark J. Rebilas-USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="13"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/17c40d368970d44adc7249861a5b572122dc09d4dc12460b7c433af271308efe/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fc614d00af342ddde358abd794218ee2a&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/17c40d368970d44adc7249861a5b572122dc09d4dc12460b7c433af271308efe/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fc614d00af342ddde358abd794218ee2a"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) shoots the ball over Atlanta Hawks guard Bogdan Bogdanovic (13) in the first quarter during