ew="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="45"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/f597cbfc48ac6697a735b2a5581f8616e6ba9741f9f68cfca317e38ffdb70794/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F5c153d8def8696bc925b64b194c88700&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/f597cbfc48ac6697a735b2a5581f8616e6ba9741f9f68cfca317e38ffdb70794/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F5c153d8def8696bc925b64b194c88700"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talks with head coach Mike Budenholzer during the first half of their Eastern Conference finals game against the Atlanta Hawks Wednesday, June 23, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wis. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="46"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/e370f12bc687b6a0357b3bdab7ce46036ced8acb5bc1dd194a3004b2bdcb47de/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F380d76d809192c27d0de61fe834919bf&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/e370f12bc687b6a0357b3bdab7ce46036ced8acb5bc1dd194a3004b2bdcb47de/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F380d76d809192c27d0de61fe834919bf"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) and Atlanta Hawks center Clint Capela (15) fall to the floor as Antetokounmpo (34) is injured on the play in the third quarter during Game 4 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs at State Farm Arena on June 29, 2021. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Brett Davis, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="47"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c44cda8942c10ba833abfc0e024211e1a740f4ef26dfe6c89965973fb0d1b2f9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fbdaab2ed7abfa01768bd7f94ca73d072&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c44cda8942c10ba833abfc0e024211e1a740f4ef26dfe6c89965973fb0d1b2f9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fbdaab2ed7abfa01768bd7f94ca73d072"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) puts up a one handed jump shot over Brooklyn Nets forward Blake Griffin (2) in the second quarter during Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Wendell Cruz, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="48"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/caafb468ef01ce86ee1777dc637e4ecbd004d58380a7d54998ee18ba4ecca3be/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F54e27416982f496742a3d4a60c08cd72&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/caafb468ef01ce86ee1777dc637e4ecbd004d58380a7d54998ee18ba4ecca3be/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F54e27416982f496742a3d4a60c08cd72"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) has his leg worked on during Game 2 of the NBA Finals against the Phoenix Suns at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021.</div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="49"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c2f75cd08bd14ed98ec46530c53b1c3202e32dba1251b693cba8d9b296f6f052/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fcf1a56561f00ab295a3b02337d2268e8&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c2f75cd08bd14ed98ec46530c53b1c3202e32dba1251b693cba8d9b296f6f052/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fcf1a56561f00ab295a3b02337d2268e8"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton to preserve the lead late in Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.<br><br>It's one of the most lasting images in NBA Finals history.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Stacy Revere, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure></div><div class="right-nav"><button class="" title="Next photo" tabindex="0" data-ylk="ct:slideshow;elm:arrow;itc:1;outcm:ct;sec:sshow;subsec:slideshow;slk:next;" data-yga="{&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;slideshow&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;arrow&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;sshow&quot;,&quot;ySubModuleName&quot;:&quot;slideshow&quot;,&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;next&quot;,&quot;yHasCommerce&quot;:false}"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" class="fill-white"><path d="M7.06.665a2.27 2.27 0 0 1 3.21 0L25.606 16 10.27 31.335c-.442.443-1.023.665-1.604.665s-1.162-.222-1.605-.665a2.27 2.27 0 0 1 0-3.21L19.185 16 7.06 3.876a2.27 2.27 0 0 1 0-3.21z"></path></svg></button></div></div><div aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">1</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><div class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Five years ago, Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Milwaukee Bucks to their first NBA championship in 50 years after he scored 50 points in the clinching Game 6 over the Phoenix Suns. <br><br>It capped an incredible playoff run that also saw him return faster than anyone thought from a hyperextended left knee he suffered during the Eastern Conference finals. <br><br>He would deliver several masterpieces throughout the playoffs and iconic NBA Finals moments.<br><br>Scroll through this gallery for all of Giannis' highlights during the 2021 postseason.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark J. Rebilas, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></div></div></div><div class="hide-vertical"><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="" data-slide-index="0" style="order:0"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/40f7e12f115997cc6d20cd933bf92a3c71f4e8e48c334448b8a28971608a0f7f/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Ffbfb2b058ff6c7101db72e2246f290e1"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">1</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Five years ago, Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Milwaukee Bucks to their first NBA championship in 50 years after he scored 50 points in the clinching Game 6 over the Phoenix Suns. <br><br>It capped an incredible playoff run that also saw him return faster than anyone thought from a hyperextended left knee he suffered during the Eastern Conference finals. <br><br>He would deliver several masterpieces throughout the playoffs and iconic NBA Finals moments.<br><br>Scroll through this gallery for all of Giannis' highlights during the 2021 postseason.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark J. Rebilas, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="1" style="order:1"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/a825d43ae192119de89e1342535ab17acfbf756d16d7ad91fc32bf1238dfc9d9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1bb0c616dab516bfa4940781743f7ba1"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">2</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton in the closing moments of Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. <br><br>The Bucks defeated the Suns, 109-103, to even the series.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="2" style="order:2"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/59a82a2d33c73b2db79f1a4c43232dc00553a737293a774a4b60fa7c3fdd7cc5/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1cedaa3e606aba34dc16a3d27587eec9"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">3</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second quarter against the Phoenix Suns during Game 4 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on Jul 14, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Jeff Hanisch, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="3" style="order:3"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/5fde4a257a5fcc8f10eb176cdd26f1cf074a7190c43291ff9776137da51de1fc/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fe12995