o highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) holds his NBA Finals trophy after the 105-98 win over the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="16" style="order:16"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/00706a36a14bcd927ec4b710aa150b167faf2d57f3286715ae3f793fb78e8599/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fe03d5bacc2ff69d5bdd9a0c401594ce8"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">17</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second half of Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. <br><br>Antetokounmpo scored 50 points as the Bucks defeated the Suns 105-98 to win the NBA championship.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="17" style="order:17"><div class="c