s during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks for a basket ahead of Phoenix Suns forward Torrey Craig (12) during the first half in Game 1 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Matt York, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="19" style="order:19"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c17f23c5cdfbb28cab1e1dae8c8f777bc35708bc49525043d8f5cd8f29c318dc/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F609d44c5a0582eb5c489cdf4452df5e8"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">20</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (right) congratulates forward Khris Middleton (22) after a basket during the third quarter against the Atlanta Hawks in Game 6 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on July 3, 2021, at State Farm Arena. <br><br>Antetokounmpo missed the last two games of the series after injuring his left knee in Game 4.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Jason Getz, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="20" style="order:20"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/08ffc173c5f3908f726d1561747887632e3e6d9c888dae9ebec6983b185d40d1/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fe97eb63ac6b07d6c016e0996f7c02575"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">21</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drive to the basket past Brooklyn Nets guard Mike James (55) during the 3rd quarter of their eastern conference semifinal playoff game at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. Photo by Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel via USA TODAY NETWORK ORG XMIT: DBY1</div><span class="caption-credit"> (Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="21" style="order:21"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/28c239e8e9bc872035d11e1f2b46b90b5d232ea149070f7f4bb8ef59b29affab/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F046e9ada69df2f428840edb771757d4a"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">22</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Injured Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo congratulates center Brook Lopez (11) during the second half of Game 5 of the Eastern Conference finals game Thursday, July 1, 2021 at Fiserv Forum. <br><br>The Milwaukee Bucks beat the Atlanta Hawks, 123-112, to take a 3-2 series lead. <br><br>Antetokounmpo missed the game with a left knee injury. <br><br>Lopez led the Bucks in scoring with 33 points. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="22" style="order:22"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/f406b5e0d3534928bef0ae4a578b9e544eac78f684716e63efb47f26f0faf1a6/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F726716e4133f90ad314a0906a1a7dcaa"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">23</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo celebrates winning the Bill Russell NBA Finals MVP Award after defeating the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 to win the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 20, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="23" style="order:23"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/007ddc688b15f8bc4f82dbdff7fcbee45fbdfde1cd84f5e255736ce9d8ee26e1/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Ff9ab2b90a3dd0d574813bc33354d7112"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">24</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) scores two of his game-high 50 points as Phoenix Suns forward Frank Kaminsky (8) tries to block the shot during the fourth quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. <br><br>The 50 points are tied for most in an NBA Finals clinching game in NBA history.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="24" style="order:24"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/bbb592d2