inals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) and Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talk during the third quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. <br><br>Antetokounmpo scored 50 and Middleton added 17 in the game.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="29" style="order:29"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/d2db1c8f2e4112d94272d09b22f11bd69c3bc37152da4214f6d20b5ff2917ba4/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F458d08bdef6c632f58d56b2a02f07c42"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">30</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) warms up before Milwaukee Bucks play the Phoenix Suns at the Phoenix Suns Arena in Game 1 of the NBA Finals in Phoenix on Tuesday, July 6, 2021. <br><br>Antetokounmpo returned to action just over a week after hyperextending his left knee in the Eastern Conference finals.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="30" style="order:30"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/e02d144c162f02a48e6b08bfbeb393ffd653b66e97c4f9d969a07d5ecefcc6fe/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F77f4f3b631b9d364c05e886a0b7ba022"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">31</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks Giannis Antetokounmpo holds the Larry O'Brien Trophy as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="31" style="order:31"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/57e04a478fd5b1c832db388f103b7edcb538bdd316d66ef09210143919c014c5/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Ff7cff0e7b3f87473ba09f8569450dfa2"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">32</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo scores two of his 26 points  against the Miami Heat during Game 1 of their Eastern Conference first-round playoff series at Fiserv Forum on May 22, 2021.<br><br>The Bucks beat the Heat, 109-107, in overtime on their way to a series sweep.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Quinn Harris, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="32" style="order:32"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/6f62d8aa85201e3317d5a939a257934e73b1a5378ab46f6da1e24fece07302a4/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F7efccee068e8d98fb7ce416260e8f8a4"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">33</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks' Giannis Antetokounmpo sets up a play against the Atlanta Hawks' Trae Young during the third quarter in Game 1 of the Eastern Conference finals at Fiserv Forum on June 23, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Patrick McDermott, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="33" style="order:33"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/4a57535cb56cab629ef52a30abe1f2bae94a51f90caf2058a3728b7cd35d64f6/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fb67e5a2c17547a95a0a3d9841228c3dc"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">34</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo dunks the ball in the third quarter against Jimmy Butler of the Miami Heat during Game 2 of their Eastern Conference first-round playoff series between the Milwaukee Bucks and the Miami Heat at Fiserv Forum on May 24, 2021.<br><br>Antetokounmpo had a game-high 31 points on 12 of 23 shooting and 13 rebounds as the Bucks crushed the Heat, 132-98, to take a 2-0 lead in the series.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Quinn Harris, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="34" style="order:34"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c1027436fc290b3f9e00c28eac8d336ed7013e113a435853814a5d996b125696/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fe9ddbedaadf6849b19600cc53b75b32d"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">35</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) lays the ball up while Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) attempts to guard him during the first half of Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. <br><br>Antetokounmpo was unstoppable in the title-clinching game, scoring nearly half of the Bucks points in the 105-98 win.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="35" style="order:35"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/3896f34b08653127df42c991f954c27a251e9bd65b76118548832c5272a578a9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F219121b30e982facaa369afb2121e08f"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">36</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) puts up a shot at the basket in the first quarter of their Eastern Conference semifinal playoff Game 4 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="36" style="order:36"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/44a434f1818c224464c2d5bd23e23fd2be69cea1a430e7e0532089c74fb8b4c6/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fc3a24ad48b028953aa2d8917af9adbdd"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">37</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drives to the basket against Brooklyn Nets point guard Mike James (55) and point guard Kyrie Irving (11) during the second quarter of Game 1 in the Eastern Conference semifinals of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 5.<br><br>Antetokounmpo scored 34 poitns but it wasn't enough as the Bucks fell 115-107 in the series opener.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Brad Penner, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="37" style="order:37"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/75526c588235ad7261c8942190fd6906f3851fd11dd7a1ac2fc8b5d6b7903cef/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Ff0da4174cd54d28c6ec09b791efc0b73"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">38</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the fourth quarter of their Eastern Conference semifinal playoff game against the Brooklyn Nets at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. <br><br>Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 34 points in the Bucks' 107-96 win in Game 4 to even the best-of-seven series at 2-2.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="38" style="order:38"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/535a9cb58453550f4137eb0f996571f0890562e157589497bb5f5d0d0abafb28/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F6c426cc5c440059dbc4af269809ee489"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">39</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals to win the championship in front of their home fans at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="39" style="order:39"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/6285e73f506a9024721c8b8adbc8ad9326aa20730b842bc67bb0cf54053c3660/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F221e61ae17ea3ef2fdfd1efaf0021ff3"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">40</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo, right, watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, a day before Game 4 of the series.<br><br>Antetokounmpo managed a left knee injury during the NBA Finals after suffering the injury in the Eastern Conference finals.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="40" style="order:40"><div class="cropped-wrapper" s