b279b387b9070b95aa79b0e7f6864"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">42</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="42" style="order:42"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/0989179e67be514cbeaf0f6c403e715eedce1c43d7c3da1b0afb6de69030d44b/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F7e83cb8025cd7ee48e073e7a7ad217ab"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">43</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.<br><br>He scored 50 points on 16 of 25 shooting, as well as 17 of 19 on free throws, plus 14 rebounds and five blocks.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="43" style="order:43"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/0dcfa69f734c0c2170234d3df8186f315541d736498a7c67bc32f38b09afc599/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F2eb9923f5ae015bd9510e3ffd5a8de9e"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">44</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="44" style="order:44"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c6c27b14c1f915168d7f0e520c9e4b848ea4d33909e535b7b22c6c73e01bba62/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fa6d4174857eda2b4eceef4934753c007"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">45</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks assistant coach Vin Baker jokes with Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021, ahead of Game 6 on July 20.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="45" style="order:45"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/f597cbfc48ac6697a735b2a5581f8616e6ba9741f9f68cfca317e38ffdb70794/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F5c153d8def8696bc925b64b194c88700"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">46</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talks with head coach Mike Budenholzer during the first half of their Eastern Conference finals game against the Atlanta Hawks Wednesday, June 23, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wis. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="46" style="order:46"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/e370f12bc687b6a0357b3bdab7ce46036ced8acb5bc1dd194a3004b2bdcb47de/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F380d76d809192c27d0de61fe834919bf"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">47</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) and Atlanta Hawks center Clint Capela (15) fall to the floor as Antetokounmpo (34) is injured on the play in the third quarter during Game 4 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs at State Farm Arena on June 29, 2021. </p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Brett Davis, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="47" style="order:47"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c44cda8942c10ba833abfc0e024211e1a740f4ef26dfe6c89965973fb0d1b2f9/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fbdaab2ed7abfa01768bd7f94ca73d072"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">48</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) puts up a one handed jump shot over Brooklyn Nets forward Blake Griffin (2) in the second quarter during Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Wendell Cruz, USA TODAY Sports)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="48" style="order:48"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/caafb468ef01ce86ee1777dc637e4ecbd004d58380a7d54998ee18ba4ecca3be/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F54e27416982f496742a3d4a60c08cd72"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">49</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) has his leg worked on during Game 2 of the NBA Finals against the Phoenix Suns at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021.</div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="vertical-photos"><div class="hidden" data-slide-index="49" style="order:49"><div class="cropped-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><img alt="" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="cropped-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/c2f75cd08bd14ed98ec46530c53b1c3202e32dba1251b693cba8d9b296f6f052/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fcf1a56561f00ab295a3b02337d2268e8"/></div><div class="slide-desc"><span class="slide-start">50</span><span class="slide-end"> / <!-- -->50</span></div><h2 class="slide-headline">Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks&#x27; 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h2><figcaption class="slide-caption"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit"><p style="margin: 0px;">Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton to preserve the lead late in Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.<br><br>It's one of the most lasting images in NBA Finals history.</p></div><span class="caption-credit"> (Stacy Revere, Getty Images)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure></div><h2 class="heading">What do you remember from the night the Bucks won in Game 6 of the NBA Finals?</h2><ul class="content-list"><li><div><p>&quot;Being at the game with my son and watching Giannis and the Bucks bring Milwaukee their first championship in 50 years.&quot; – Todd Marohl, Menomonee Falls</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;My three kids and grandson being at the game together and the emotions of finally being on top after all the down years!! Special moment!&quot; – Jamie Conom, Sun Prairie</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I was glad that they won and wondered if they could defend their title in a &#x27;normal&#x27; season that wasn&#x27;t affected by COVID-19.&quot; – Michael Izard, Middle River, Maryland</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Feeling like I was in 12 again in 1970-71. Was in the arena for that clincher. Had a sign [that said] Bullets are shot! Made the paper next day.&quot; – Jerry Vales, McHenry, Illinois</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I was at the game with my son, then age 25. It was the sports spectating event of our lives!&quot; – Mike Peters, Oconomowoc</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Being able to attend the game with my son and seeing how charged up and excited the fans were both inside and outside Fiserv.&quot; – Tom Wimmer, Argonne</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I was there with my then 16-year-old son. We flew in from our home in Boulder, Colorado, to see Game 6 in person and oh was it worth the trip. Epic night!&quot; – Jason Gerlach, Boulder, Colorado</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I watched Game 6 in the Deer District, on the old Bradley Center lot. Huge crowd, a pretty close game and then pure pandemonium when the Bucks won it.&quot; – Bill Cole, Menomonee Falls</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;The Full Buck Moon a few nights after the big game. Very appropriate timing.&quot; – Pete Schmidt, Nolensville, Tennessee</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I was at Fiserv Plaza with thousands of fans. The atmosphere was electric and the group went crazy at the final buzzer. It was amazing!&quot; - Mac, Milwaukee</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Welcomed our first child May 2021. Watched all of the playoffs with sleepless infant. House asleep night of championship, celebrated silently.&quot; – Nathaniel, Appleton</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I remember being in the Deer District and standing in disbelief as the first sky cam shot showed the crowd downtown. Chills!&quot; – Nick Koss, Franklin</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;For my wife and I, game 1 vs. Miami at the Deer District was our first big outing post COVID. A sunny, daytime game with others!&quot; – Jason, West Allis</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Giannis&#x27; big game in the deciding game.&quot; – Kurt, River Falls</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;I was driving back to Arizona from Wisconsin and watching game 6 in Texas at a packed bar but only two tables watching the game. Ours and Suns fans! Fun!&quot; – John Francois, Phoenix, Arizona</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Being in the building for the last timeout when everyone knew the Bucks had the game won. Unreal.&quot; – Pat, Columbia, Missouri</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Was overnight in Reno, Nevada, on a trip to Vegas with kids. Told them Bucks stories and finished with &#x27;Bucks in 6.&#x27; Had to bet on Bucks in 6 of course. WINNER. Wouldn&#x27;t cash the ticket unless I could keep it.&quot; – Mark Ellis, Lebanon, New Hampshire</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Being there to witness Game 6 in person with my son, who was 20 years old at the time, and experiencing the championship events is a lasting memory.&quot; – Garry, <a data-ylk="" data-yga="{&quot;yHasCommerce&quot;:false}" href="/nba/teams/houston/" rel="">Houston</a>, Texas</p></div></li><li><div><p>&quot;Being there with my son - greatest night of our lives. Then heading to the Ambassador where we joined my wife and were up until 2 in the morning!&quot; – Paul Krueger, Sheboygan</p></div></li></ul><div class="slideshow hide-slideshow"><div class="slideshow-wrap related-side"><div class="left-nav"><button class="hidden md:block" title="Previous photo" tabindex="0" data-ylk="ct:slideshow;elm:arrow;itc:1;outcm:ct;sec:sshow;subsec:slideshow;slk:previous;" data-yga="{&quot;yContentType&quot;:&quot;slideshow&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;arrow&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;sshow&quot;,&quot;ySubModuleName&quot;:&quot;slideshow&quot;,&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;previous&quot;,&quot;yHasCommerce&quot;:false}"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" class="fill-white"><path d="M22.72.665a2.27 2.27 0 0 0-3.21 0L4.175 16 19.51 31.335c.442.443 1.023.665 1.604.665s1.162-.222 1.605-.665a2.27 2.27 0 0 0 0-3.21L10.596 16 22.72 3.876a2.27 2.27 0 0 0 0-3.21z"></path></svg></button></div><div class="slide-photos" id="_R_h8jplh9av5ubsqlb_"><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="true"><div class="snap-start snap-always" data-slide-index="0"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/86fe1b04ee5bf60a9e54012a137a9def31c541c2fdb3c7c47e8638ca86412051/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fbc59e6e47475e4e3661ff9c0cd8d872a&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/86fe1b04ee5bf60a9e54012a137a9def31c541c2fdb3c7c47e8638ca86412051/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2Fbc59e6e47475e4e3661ff9c0cd8d872a"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) and Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) holding the Larry O'Brien NBA Championship Trophyafter the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="1"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/bb906d1519875d138ff1789471aba072d533a574d21d75b3c151c4203f5769d2/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F8c656d91ca6d8d8957e2447567e41b14&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/bb906d1519875d138ff1789471aba072d533a574d21d75b3c151c4203f5769d2/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F8c656d91ca6d8d8957e2447567e41b14"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) holds his NBA FINALS MVP Trophy as Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) holds the Larry O'Brien NBA Championship Trophy after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="2"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/dc5fe34596c8acea6406c12de3e3e3a74a38a859a53100688bda54c596ce8313/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F96cdac6c3d57d7123b535e262477f6d1&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/dc5fe34596c8acea6406c12de3e3e3a74a38a859a53100688bda54c596ce8313/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F96cdac6c3d57d7123b535e262477f6d1"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22), left, holds the Larry O'Brien trophy and Giannis Antetokounmpo has the Finals MVP trophy after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals on Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.</div><span class="caption-credit"> (Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel)</span></div></figcaption></div></figure><figure class="slide-photo" data-inview="false"><div class="snap-start snap-always hidden" data-slide-index="3"><div class="letterboxed-img-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9"><div class="letterbox-bg" style="background-image:url(&quot;https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/991fd5e7604941763478deeba4fe322dc535c4d36e5ce4192ac317ba71f2ca0d/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1751cced4d52b757a85bd7f215e65194&quot;)"></div><img alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="letterboxed-img" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/991fd5e7604941763478deeba4fe322dc535c4d36e5ce4192ac317ba71f2ca0d/lightyear_networkapi/resizefill_w976%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fmilwaukee_journal_sentinel_national_slideshows_156%2F1751cced4d52b757a85bd7f215e65194"/></div><figcaption class="caption-node"><div style="max-height:none;overflow:visible"><div class="fig-credit">Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) and Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) hug while holding the Larry O'Brien NBA Championship Trophyafter the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</div><span class="capti